## Understanding Super Heinz Flag Bets
A Super Heinz Flag combines 7 selections into 162 separate bets, extending the standard Super Heinz format by adding 42 Single Stakes About pairings. The traditional Super Heinz contains 120 bets from 6 selections, but the Flag version requires one additional selection and incorporates protective pairing mechanisms. This betting structure originated in horse racing where multiple winners across a card generate returns even when several selections lose.
### Super Heinz Flag Composition
| Component | Number of Bets |
|-----------|----------------|
| Doubles | 21 |
| Trebles | 35 |
| Four-folds | 35 |
| Five-folds | 21 |
| Six-folds | 7 |
| Seven-fold Accumulator | 1 |
| Single Stakes About | 42 |
| **Total** | **162** |
The 42 Single Stakes About bets distinguish the Flag from the standard Super Heinz. Each Single Stakes About pairs two selections, creating 21 doubles with stakes that apply twice across the combinations. If both horses in a paired bet win, the stake rolls from the first winner onto the second, generating enhanced returns compared to standalone doubles.
### Each Way Super Heinz Flag
Activating each way doubles the bet count to 324 by placing both win and place stakes on every combination. This option costs twice the standard total stake but provides returns when selections finish in placing positions without winning. For a 10p stake per bet, the each way total stake reaches £32.40 (162 win bets at 10p plus 162 place bets at 10p).
The Super Heinz Flag requires at least two winning selections to generate any return, though maximum profit demands all seven selections winning. The calculator processes these 162 combinations to show exact stake requirements and potential returns based on entered odds.
## 162 Bets Explained - Complete Breakdown
A super heinz flag calculator processes 162 individual bets derived from 7 selections. The composition includes 21 doubles, 35 trebles, 35 four-folds, 21 five-folds, 7 six-folds, and 1 seven-fold accumulator, totaling 120 standard combination bets. An additional 42 Single Stakes About bets provide insurance coverage, bringing the complete total to 162 bets.
### Combination Breakdown by Type
The standard Super Heinz structure generates 120 bets across six combination tiers. Doubles pair every possible two-selection combination from the original 7 selections, producing 21 doubles. Trebles group three selections in all possible arrangements, creating 35 trebles. Four-folds combine four selections across 35 different permutations, while five-folds generate 21 combinations of five selections each. Six-folds produce 7 bets using six selections, and the single seven-fold accumulator requires all 7 selections to win.
| Combination Type | Number of Bets | Selections Per Bet |
|-----------------|----------------|-------------------|
| Doubles | 21 | 2 |
| Trebles | 35 | 3 |
